[quote="Jeysie"]

The impression I get is that &quot;flavor&quot; is the entire name of the game. Any character can have enough power to get stuff done, especially since the system seems very heavily weighted towards letting people succeed the majority of the time even if it&#39;s with a plot twist. So it&#39;s more a question of creating characters that are thematically cohesive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

[/quote]

It feels the way Marvel Heroic Roleplaying did. (Which makes sense since Cam was involved in both) I ran the Breakout adventure a couple of times at a con with folks picking from a big list of pregens. I don&#39;t remember the whole team, but I do recall once there was a team with Kitty Pryde and the Hulk on the team, and both characters contributed equally to the story.

 SC seems very story focused, so it doesn&#39;t matter that Wraith and Fanatic operate on different power levels. Like if there&#39;s a giant robot attacking the city.(1)&nbsp; Fanatic&#39;s action is &quot;I swoop down from the sky and smite the giant robot with my flaming sword&quot; and Wraith&#39;s is &quot;from the shadows, I throw a knife at an important joint actuator&quot; they&#39;re having just as much impact on the story.&nbsp;&nbsp; 

(1) As seen in Sentinel Comics Side-By-Side Issue #43 - &quot;It&#39;s Hard to Be A Saint In Rook City&quot;&nbsp;
